From: RNSBox <rnsbox@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] riscv: dts: sophgo: program the SLIP UART clock at probe time

Assigning a PLL rate on the clock-controller node runs in of_clk_init(),
before the timers are up; the PLL lock poll never returns and the EVB
stops right after "legacy bootconsole [sbi0] enabled". This happened
with both the disppll and the cam0pll assignment.

Move the assignment to the uart2 consumer node. of_clk_set_defaults()
then runs at probe time, after the clock framework and the timers are
ready, and the 8250 reads the resulting 96 MHz when it probes.

UART1/UART2 take cam0pll as their baud clock (previous patch). 96 MHz
makes the modem 2 Mbaud exact; clk_cam0_200 stays on the crystal for the
console and disppll (AXI/CPU) is not touched at all.

--- a/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
+++ b/arch/riscv/boot/dts/sophgo/sg2000-duomodule01-evb.dts
@@ -304,9 +304,6 @@
  * this mux in a state Linux can rely on, so pin parent and rate here.
  */
 &clk {
-	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0_200>;
-	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_DISPPLL>;
-	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
 };
 
 /*
@@ -325,6 +322,11 @@
  * and the UART card in Settings shows it. UART1 is muxed by S31slip; the
  * other pads need a board-specific fmux setup before use. */
 &uart2 {
+	/* Programmed at probe: of_clk_init runs before the timers, and the
+	 * PLL lock poll never returns there. */
+	assigned-clocks = <&clk CLK_CAM0PLL>;
+	assigned-clock-parents = <&clk CLK_MIPIMPLL>;
+	assigned-clock-rates = <96000000>;
 	pinctrl-names = "default";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&uart2_cfg>;
 	status = "okay";
